### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### Variables pour les tests (à modifier selon vos besoins)
@testControllerId = web-abc123
@testControllerType = WEB
@testHardwareControllerId = hw-pad-01

# ============================================
# 1) CONTROLLERS - REGISTER
# ============================================

### 1.1. Register controller (Succès - WEB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "controller_id": "{{testControllerId}}",
  "controller_type": "{{testControllerType}}"
}

### 1.2. Register controller (Succès - HARDWARE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "controller_id": "{{testHardwareControllerId}}",
  "controller_type": "HARDWARE"
}

### 1.3. Register controller (Succès - type par défaut WEB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "controller_id": "web-default-type"
}

### 1.4. Register controller (Succès - déjà existant, idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "controller_id": "{{testControllerId}}",
  "controller_type": "{{testControllerType}}"
}

### 1.5. Register controller - Erreur: controller_id manquant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "controller_type": "WEB"
}

### 1.6. Register controller - Erreur: controller_id vide
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "controller_id": "",
  "controller_type": "WEB"
}

### 1.7. Register controller - Erreur: controller_type invalide
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "controller_id": "web-invalid-type",
  "controller_type": "MOBILE"
}

# ============================================
# 2) CONTROLLERS - AVAILABLE
# ============================================

### 2.1. Lire les controllers disponibles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/controllers/available

